[gd_scene format=3]

; The Bore, west of the Calving (map offset (116.5, -71)): a mining machine frozen mid-bore, its drill head driven into
; the rock at the west end of its hall. A pilgrim shrine in the hall. Beside the drill head, a shaft drops into the
; chamber it was cutting: the Drill relic waits at its end, and there is no climbing back up the shaft. A wall of
; cracked rock seals the chamber from a tunnel under the hall, whose steps come up through a hole in the hall's floor:
; seen first from the tunnel side, the cracked wall is what the Drill is for. The chamber's floor is cracked too, over
; the way down to the Fissure (sealed: not built yet).

